Package: superscreener
Type: Package
Title: Cross-Validated Variable Screening with a Price per Variable
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nolan", "Gunter", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "nola@berkeley.edu"),
    person("Alan", "Hubbard", role = "aut"))
Description: SuperScreener chooses both the screening rule and the number of
    variables for a binary-outcome prediction model. Candidates are ranking
    screeners (univariate likelihood ratio, lasso entry order, random forest
    importance, their consensus, Spearman correlation) at a grid of budgets K,
    plus screeners that set their own size (screen.glmnet, screen.corP, lasso at
    lambda.1se, stability selection). Each candidate's selected set is passed to
    the same Super Learner, and the cross-validation selector picks the candidate
    with the smallest cross-validated risk plus a price per variable used. The
    package also provides nested cross-validation of the whole procedure with
    influence-curve intervals for the AUC, selection-stability summaries, and the
    simulation design used in the accompanying dissertation chapter.
URL: https://github.com/nolangunter/superscreener
BugReports: https://github.com/nolangunter/superscreener/issues
